== the bump ladder, on fixtures ==
ok  unchanged -> none
ok  control added -> minor
ok  control removed -> major
ok  control renamed -> major
ok  prose edited -> patch
ok  nested control enhancements are counted as ids
ok  the real catalog/bump.yaml and rule.yaml parse with the standard library
ok  (1) the predecessor's file name is read at v1.0.0, not from the tree: a rename computes none
ok  (1) ...and a rename carrying a removed control computes major against the tag's bytes
ok  (2) v1.1.0 declared minor over v1.0.0 is admitted
ok  (2) v1.0.1 declared minor is refused: the tag is a patch increment
ok  (2) v2.0.0 declared minor is refused: the tag is a major increment
ok  (2) --tree derives v1.1.0 from the declared minor and admits it
ok  (2) --tree refuses a declared none while the tree carries a minor
ok  (2) v1.0.1 declared none is refused: no tag carries none
ok  (2) --tree under a declared none admits an unchanged tree: no release is queued
ok  (3) a --no-tags clone of a released repository is refused, not graded as a first release
ok  (3) ...and --tree refuses the same way, not exit 3
ok  (3) a clone of a repository that never released takes the first-release path
ok  (3) ...and --tree names the tree's own publishedVersion as that first release

